---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import Section from "../components/layout/Section.astro";
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms and conditions for using the Apoti Development Association website and making donations."
>
  <Section background="white" padding="lg">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose prose-gray">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold text-gray-900">
        Terms of Service
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
        Last updated: May 16, 2026 · Effective: May 16, 2026
      </p>

      <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing or using the Apoti Development Association (ADA) website at <strong
          >apotidev.org</strong
        >, you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree
        to these terms, please do not use the website. ADA is a registered
        non-profit organisation in the Republic of Cameroon (Registration N°
        415/G.37/D14/VolI/SAAJP).
      </p>

      <h2>2. Donations</h2>
      <p>
        All donations made through this website are voluntary contributions to
        ADA's charitable programs. By completing a donation, you confirm that:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>You are the authorised holder of the payment method used.</li>
        <li>The funds are not derived from any illegal activity.</li>
        <li>You are making the donation of your own free will.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Receipts:</strong> A receipt for your records will be emailed after
        your payment is confirmed. Donations to ADA are <strong
          >not tax-deductible</strong
        > in Canada, the US, the UK, or the EU, as ADA is registered only as an NGO
        in Cameroon. ADA does not currently issue tax-deductible receipts in those
        jurisdictions.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Refund policy:</strong> Donations are generally non-refundable, as
        funds are allocated to programs promptly. However, if a donation was made
        in error (e.g., duplicate charge, incorrect amount, or unauthorised use of
        a payment method), please contact us at <a
          href="mailto:info@apotidev.org">info@apotidev.org</a
        > within <strong>30 days</strong> of the transaction. We will review all refund
        requests in good faith and process eligible refunds within 5–10 business days.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Monthly donations:</strong> You may cancel your recurring monthly
        donation at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:info@apotidev.org"
          >info@apotidev.org</a
        >. Cancellations take effect at the end of the current billing cycle. No
        cancellation fees apply.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Donor Accounts</h2>
      <p>
        You may create a donor account to track your giving history and contact
        ADA about monthly donations. You are responsible for maintaining the
        confidentiality of your account credentials and for all activity that
        occurs under your account. Please notify us immediately of any
        unauthorised use of your account.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Acceptable Use</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to use this website only for lawful purposes and in a manner
        consistent with its charitable mission. You may not:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Attempt to gain unauthorised access to any part of the website or its
          underlying systems.
        </li>
        <li>
          Use the website to transmit harmful, fraudulent, or malicious content.
        </li>
        <li>Interfere with the website's operation or other users' access.</li>
        <li>
          Misrepresent your identity, affiliation, or the purpose of a donation.
        </li>
        <li>
          Use automated tools to scrape, crawl, or extract data from the website
          without prior written permission.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>
        All content on this website — including text, photographs, videos,
        logos, and design — is the property of Apoti Development Association or
        its content contributors, unless otherwise noted. You may share links to
        our content and use brief excerpts for non-commercial purposes with
        attribution. You may not reproduce, distribute, or create derivative
        works without our prior written permission.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Third-Party Links</h2>
      <p>
        Our website may contain links to third-party websites (e.g., Stripe,
        social media platforms). These links are provided for convenience only.
        ADA is not responsible for the content, privacy practices, or terms of
        any third-party website.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
      <p>
        ADA provides this website "as is" and "as available" without warranties
        of any kind, express or implied. We do not warrant that the website will
        be uninterrupted, error-free, or free of viruses or other harmful
        components.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, ADA shall not be
        liable for any indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages
        arising from your use of the website, including but not limited to
        service interruptions, data loss, or errors in content. ADA's total
        liability for any claim arising from these terms shall not exceed the
        amount of your most recent donation to ADA.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Governing Law and Dispute Resolution</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms of Service are governed by the laws of the Republic of
        Cameroon. However, we recognise that our donors are located
        internationally. For disputes that cannot be resolved informally, we
        commit to good-faith mediation before pursuing formal legal proceedings.
        If you are a consumer in the European Union or the United Kingdom, you
        retain the benefit of any mandatory consumer protection laws that apply
        in your jurisdiction, which these terms do not override.
      </p>
      <p>
        To raise a concern or dispute, please contact us first at <a
          href="mailto:info@apotidev.org">info@apotidev.org</a
        >. We aim to resolve all concerns within 10 business days.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Changes to These Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms of Service from time to time. When we do, we
        will update the "Last updated" date at the top of this page. For
        significant changes, we will notify registered users by email at least
        14 days before the changes take effect. Continued use of the website
        after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>For questions about these terms, please contact:</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Apoti Development Association</strong><br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:info@apotidev.org">info@apotidev.org</a><br />
        Website: <a href="https://apotidev.org">apotidev.org</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</PageLayout>
